  "notes": "Backend-declared, unmeasured by CERE. SGLang sglang-t4 owns batching, KV cache and EAGLE speculative decoding (steps 3, topk 1, draft tokens 4); EAGLE is declared lossless by the backend and has not been measured. NVFP4 weights and fp8_e4m3 KV cache, so not a reference numerical mode. Rows are concurrent CERE requests (1-4, up to max_running_requests 4), not native batch rows; rows 3-4 exercised only on cere-bench-g0, see bench/reports; sglang-t4 capped at 2 by its config. Tool calls are backend-declared (SGLang qwen3_coder parser; unmeasured by CERE); logprobs pass through with top_logprobs up to 20. top_k, frequency/presence/repetition penalties and logit_bias are forwarded verbatim (declared, unmeasured; under NEXTN speculation top-k/top-p apply sequentially and penalties count once per verify step after the first token); min_p and seed are refused (M2.7 D9). Grammar (M2.8) is backend-declared: SGLang's xgrammar 0.2.1 backend enforces response_format json_object/json_schema (dialect json-schema-2020-12/xgrammar-0.2.1, the listed keywords only; numeric bounds only on integer schemas in enforced forms), top-level regex and ebnf, and tool_choice required/named or a strict tool (tool_calls_constrained); one constraint per request, greedy or sampled, rows as text decoding; CERE forwards the client's bytes and refuses what the keyword list and format set exclude. Seeded sampling is unsupported. Image input (data:image/png and data:image/jpeg base64 URLs in user content parts, at most 4 images, 1,024 tokens per image, 2,048 per request) is backend-declared and unmeasured by CERE: SGLang decodes, resizes and encodes the images. Not a throughput or capacity claim.",
